#: ../source/notebooks/customer_choice/bayesian_blp.ipynb:110012
#: 9ccbb23bca5b43b5a8d7ad84fad5f460
msgid ""
"**BayesianBLP** is a structural random-coefficients logit on aggregate "
"shares: the Bayesian reformulation of Berry, Levinsohn & Pakes (1995) "
"following Jiang, Manchanda & Rossi (2009). Reach for it when:"
msgstr ""
"**BayesianBLP** es un logit estructural de coeficientes aleatorios sobre "
"cuotas agregadas: la reformulación bayesiana de Berry, Levinsohn & Pakes "
"(1995) siguiendo a Jiang, Manchanda & Rossi (2009). Recurra a él cuando:"

#: ../source/notebooks/customer_choice/bayesian_blp.ipynb:110014
#: 190c2c209afa4ffaa937fb0e55d3bdc3
msgid "You have **aggregate market shares** (not individual transactions)."
msgstr ""
"Tiene **cuotas de mercado agregadas** (no transacciones individuales)."

#: ../source/notebooks/customer_choice/bayesian_blp.ipynb:110015
#: 2621b085d74844c7a5b7cb5002c4590d
msgid "You need structurally grounded **cross-price substitution patterns**."
msgstr ""
"Necesita **patrones de sustitución de precios cruzados** con fundamento "
"estructural."

#: ../source/notebooks/customer_choice/bayesian_blp.ipynb:110016
#: 42bc522b1f884f09a985add9d56cf15e
msgid ""
"Prices may be **endogenous** (set by firms who observe unobserved demand "
"shocks) and you have **cost or rival-characteristic instruments** to "
"correct the bias."
msgstr ""
"Los precios pueden ser **endógenos** (fijados por empresas que observan "
"choques de demanda no observados) y usted tiene **instrumentos de costos o "
"de características de los rivales** para corregir el sesgo."

#: ../source/notebooks/customer_choice/bayesian_blp.ipynb:110018
#: 9891c8b9108b4efb9fc35d824d0fe884
msgid ""
"You want **full posterior uncertainty** on elasticities and "
"counterfactual shares, with correct propagation through the structural "
"demand model."
msgstr ""
"Quiere **incertidumbre posterior completa** sobre las elasticidades y las "
"cuotas contrafactuales, con una propagación correcta a través del modelo "
"estructural de demanda."

#: ../source/notebooks/customer_choice/bayesian_blp.ipynb:110021
#: cc912abc44de4e3db573ba3a84fcd3a4
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"The Bayesian formulation replaces the classical BLP contraction mapping +"
" GMM with a joint posterior over preference parameters and the latent "
"demand shocks $\\xi_{jt}$. Hierarchical pooling across regions becomes "
"cheap, and the credible intervals stay honest under weak instruments."
msgstr ""
"La formulación bayesiana reemplaza el mapeo de contracción clásico de BLP + "
"GMM por una posterior conjunta sobre los parámetros de preferencias y los "
"choques latentes de demanda $\\xi_{jt}$. La agrupación jerárquica entre "
"regiones se vuelve económica, y los intervalos creíbles se mantienen "
"honestos con instrumentos débiles."

#: ../source/notebooks/customer_choice/bayesian_blp.ipynb:120002
#: e67942514c2e400e8f2bda6a3738b495
msgid "1. Synthetic data: a BLP-style aggregate share panel"
msgstr "1. Datos sintéticos: un panel de cuotas agregadas al estilo BLP"

#: ../source/notebooks/customer_choice/bayesian_blp.ipynb:120004
#: 1a7b201648854407b790f200637eacf5
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"We use `generate_blp_panel` to create a synthetic panel with known true "
"parameters. The data-generating process produces a joint $(\\eta_{jt}, "
"\\tilde{\\xi}_{jt})$ shock so that prices are endogenous: estimation "
"without instruments will bias the price coefficient toward zero."
msgstr ""
"Usamos `generate_blp_panel` para crear un panel sintético con parámetros "
"verdaderos conocidos. El proceso generador de datos produce un choque "
"conjunto $(\\eta_{jt}, \\tilde{\\xi}_{jt})$ de modo que los precios son "
"endógenos: la estimación sin instrumentos sesgará el coeficiente de precio "
"hacia cero."

#: ../source/notebooks/customer_choice/bayesian_blp.ipynb:120006
#: 107d90dad30d42e085c68aa3221731db
msgid ""
"The returned DataFrame is in long format: one row per (market, product), "
"with the outside good as a row labelled `'outside'`. The `truth` "
"dictionary records the DGP parameters we will try to recover."
msgstr ""
"El DataFrame devuelto está en formato largo: una fila por (mercado, "
"producto), con el bien externo como una fila etiquetada `'outside'`. El "
"diccionario `truth` registra los parámetros del DGP que intentaremos "
"recuperar."

#: ../source/notebooks/customer_choice/bayesian_blp.ipynb:120008
#: 354693ea48fd4c4ebf1df41a149c704c
#, python-format
msgid ""
"**Market semantics.** A BLP \"market\" is a `(region, period)` cell: the "
"unit at which shares and prices are observed. The model treats markets as"
" exchangeable unless you tell it otherwise. Pass `time_col=\"period\"` to"
" `BayesianBLP` to expose `period` as a first-class coordinate. Then "
"`counterfactual_shares` and `elasticities` accept `periods=` / `regions=`"
" coord-label arguments so you can phrase questions like \"raise prod_0 "
"price by 10% in periods 10–20\" directly. This notebook turns that on at "
"construction so the time-targeted counterfactual section near the end "
"just works."
msgstr ""
"**Semántica del mercado.** Un \"mercado\" de BLP es una celda `(region, "
"period)`: la unidad en la que se observan las cuotas y los precios. El "
"modelo trata los mercados como intercambiables a menos que se indique lo "
"contrario. Pase `time_col=\"period\"` a `BayesianBLP` para exponer `period` "
"como una coordenada de primera clase. Entonces `counterfactual_shares` y "
"`elasticities` aceptan los argumentos de etiquetas de coordenadas `periods=`"
" / `regions=`, de modo que puede formular preguntas como \"aumentar el "
"precio de prod_0 en un 10% en los períodos 10–20\" directamente. Este "
"cuaderno lo activa en la construcción para que la sección de contrafactuales"
" dirigidos en el tiempo, cerca del final, funcione sin más."

#: ../source/notebooks/customer_choice/bayesian_blp.ipynb:150002
#: 53a65673c1764e37ac43b9470d33ae32
msgid "2. Model specification and prior predictive check"
msgstr "2. Especificación del modelo y chequeo predictivo previo"

#: ../source/notebooks/customer_choice/bayesian_blp.ipynb:150004
#: 62de15f0a94b413db571af4432c91f7a
msgid "We instantiate `BayesianBLP` with:"
msgstr "Instanciamos `BayesianBLP` con:"

#: ../source/notebooks/customer_choice/bayesian_blp.ipynb:150005
#: fcc6714d70a8499dacac38092149387d
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"`random_coef_on=[\"price\", \"x_0\", \"x_1\"]`: a 3-dimensional consumer "
"taste vector $\\bm{\\nu}_i \\in \\mathbb{R}^3$. Each component is a "
"standardised draw that scales heterogeneity on one covariate: price "
"sensitivity ($\\sigma_\\alpha$), and the two product characteristics "
"($\\sigma_{\\beta_0}, \\sigma_{\\beta_1}$). With 3 random coefficients "
"the model fits genuine multi-dimensional taste profiles rather than "
"collapsing to scalar price sensitivity."
msgstr ""
"`random_coef_on=[\"price\", \"x_0\", \"x_1\"]`: un vector de gustos del "
"consumidor de 3 dimensiones $\\bm{\\nu}_i \\in \\mathbb{R}^3$. Cada "
"componente es una muestra estandarizada que escala la heterogeneidad en una "
"covariable: la sensibilidad al precio ($\\sigma_\\alpha$) y las dos "
"características del producto ($\\sigma_{\\beta_0}, \\sigma_{\\beta_1}$). Con"
" 3 coeficientes aleatorios el modelo ajusta perfiles de gustos genuinamente "
"multidimensionales en lugar de colapsar a una sensibilidad escalar al "
"precio."

#: ../source/notebooks/customer_choice/bayesian_blp.ipynb:150006
#: ece1e840262940eaac8342c3b82585fd
msgid ""
"`instruments=truth['instrument_cols']`: enables the price-endogeneity "
"correction."
msgstr ""
"`instruments=truth['instrument_cols']`: activa la corrección de endogeneidad"
" del precio."

#: ../source/notebooks/customer_choice/bayesian_blp.ipynb:150007
#: f9295c3bee764a359d4f2584d4abc38c
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"`n_mc_draws=200`: Owen-scrambled Halton draws filling $[0,1]^3$ and "
"mapped to $\\mathcal{N}(0, I_3)$. The rule of thumb is roughly 100 draws "
"per random-coefficient dimension; we use 200 for $D=3$."
msgstr ""
"`n_mc_draws=200`: muestras de Halton con aleatorización de Owen que llenan "
"$[0,1]^3$ y se transforman a $\\mathcal{N}(0, I_3)$. La regla general es "
"aproximadamente 100 muestras por dimensión de coeficiente aleatorio; usamos "
"200 para $D=3$."

#: ../source/notebooks/customer_choice/bayesian_blp.ipynb:150009
#: 886bcb469326475e8508bc4ce033101a
msgid ""
"A prior predictive check confirms that the priors put mass on shares "
"plausible for scanner data (all predicted shares fall in [0, 1] and sum "
"to 1 per market)."
msgstr ""
"Un chequeo predictivo previo confirma que los priors asignan masa a cuotas "
"plausibles para datos de escáner (todas las cuotas predichas están en [0, 1]"
" y suman 1 por mercado)."

#: ../source/notebooks/customer_choice/bayesian_blp.ipynb:170002
#: 8538fff49dca4d73ac596e0cc5bb9701
msgid "The Halton grid attached to the model"
msgstr "La cuadrícula de Halton asociada al modelo"

#: ../source/notebooks/customer_choice/bayesian_blp.ipynb:170004
#: ddfd74c2057e49d4a2e53b3ac4eb57c1
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Constructing `BayesianBLP` materialises a Halton grid as `model._halton` "
"of shape `(n_mc_draws, n_random)`. With `random_coef_on=[\"price\", "
"\"x_0\", \"x_1\"]` that shape is `(200, 3)`: each row is one consumer "
"type, each column is the standardised $\\mathcal{N}(0, 1)$ draw for one "
"taste dimension. The model sees this exact grid on every MCMC iteration, "
"which makes the random-coefficient logit a *quadrature* approximation "
"rather than a Monte Carlo one: the grid is data, the parameters "
"$(\\alpha, \\sigma_\\alpha, \\beta, \\sigma_\\beta, \\xi)$ are what get "
"sampled."
msgstr ""
"Al construir `BayesianBLP` se materializa una cuadrícula de Halton como "
"`model._halton` con forma `(n_mc_draws, n_random)`. Con "
"`random_coef_on=[\"price\", \"x_0\", \"x_1\"]` esa forma es `(200, 3)`: cada"
" fila es un tipo de consumidor y cada columna es la muestra estandarizada "
"$\\mathcal{N}(0, 1)$ de una dimensión de gusto. El modelo ve exactamente "
"esta cuadrícula en cada iteración de MCMC, lo que hace del logit de "
"coeficientes aleatorios una aproximación por *cuadratura* en lugar de una de"
" Monte Carlo: la cuadrícula son datos, y los parámetros $(\\alpha, "
"\\sigma_\\alpha, \\beta, \\sigma_\\beta, \\xi)$ son lo que se muestrea."

#: ../source/notebooks/customer_choice/bayesian_blp.ipynb:170006
#: 90bd221d32e641bfbff4b9f880d382e1
msgid ""
"Every per-consumer analysis later in the notebook reaches into this "
"array. Code like"
msgstr ""
"Todo análisis por consumidor más adelante en el cuaderno recurre a este "
"arreglo. Un código como"

#: ../source/notebooks/customer_choice/bayesian_blp.ipynb:170014
#: 5d6970747b984556851acad9c790b30e
msgid ""
"extracts each taste component as a concrete numeric vector of length "
"`n_mc_draws`. The cell below shows what the grid looks like for this fit."
msgstr ""
"extrae cada componente de gusto como un vector numérico concreto de longitud"
" `n_mc_draws`. La celda de abajo muestra cómo se ve la cuadrícula para este "
"ajuste."

#: ../source/notebooks/customer_choice/bayesian_blp.ipynb:200002
#: 6cc6130903ca4798b70c99742da70ed6
msgid "3. Fitting the model with instruments"
msgstr "3. Ajuste del modelo con instrumentos"

#: ../source/notebooks/customer_choice/bayesian_blp.ipynb:200004
#: 9bee2f0eb9b04923b0fe147c49cf5167
msgid ""
"The model is fit with the `nutpie` backend. We use small draw counts here"
" for speed. In practice use `draws=2000, tune=2000, chains=4`."
msgstr ""
"El modelo se ajusta con el backend `nutpie`. Aquí usamos pocas muestras por "
"rapidez. En la práctica use `draws=2000, tune=2000, chains=4`."

#: ../source/notebooks/customer_choice/bayesian_blp.ipynb:230002
#: 1939c6a90f504c19b6458b1618daaad1
msgid "4. Posterior summary and parameter recovery"
msgstr "4. Resumen de la posterior y recuperación de parámetros"

#: ../source/notebooks/customer_choice/bayesian_blp.ipynb:230004
#: 38eedea70c1e4790852450359f2de0a5
msgid ""
"We check whether the fitted posterior recovers the known DGP parameters. "
"The key structural parameters are:"
msgstr ""
"Revisamos si la posterior ajustada recupera los parámetros conocidos del "
"DGP. Los parámetros estructurales clave son:"

#: ../source/notebooks/customer_choice/bayesian_blp.ipynb:230006
#: ab0a983857af42df8986ae27bfa0b8ca
msgid ""
"`alpha_r`: the price coefficient; should be negative and close to the "
"true value."
msgstr ""
"`alpha_r`: el coeficiente de precio; debería ser negativo y cercano al valor"
" verdadero."

#: ../source/notebooks/customer_choice/bayesian_blp.ipynb:230007
#: f0441c41a02f447ab6a6bc289eacc742
msgid "`beta_r`: characteristic utility weights; should recover `true_beta`."
msgstr ""
"`beta_r`: los pesos de utilidad de las características; debería recuperar "
"`true_beta`."

#: ../source/notebooks/customer_choice/bayesian_blp.ipynb:230008
#: c826c261c4bf43959f641215e1793dc0
msgid ""
"`sigma_random`: a length-3 vector with one entry per random-coefficient "
"dimension. Entries should recover `(sigma_alpha, sigma_beta[0], "
"sigma_beta[1])` from the DGP."
msgstr ""
"`sigma_random`: un vector de longitud 3 con una entrada por cada dimensión "
"de coeficiente aleatorio. Las entradas deberían recuperar `(sigma_alpha, "
"sigma_beta[0], sigma_beta[1])` del DGP."

#: ../source/notebooks/customer_choice/bayesian_blp.ipynb:230009
#: ecc2a2e63a664cb7b225afbd7f02330e
msgid ""
"`rho_price_xi`: the endogeneity correlation; a posterior away from zero "
"confirms that price is endogenous."
msgstr ""
"`rho_price_xi`: la correlación de endogeneidad; una posterior alejada de "
"cero confirma que el precio es endógeno."

#: ../source/notebooks/customer_choice/bayesian_blp.ipynb:260002
#: 61c86132c94f4ae9b6f01082653303f5
msgid "5. Endogeneity correction: IV vs. no-IV"
msgstr "5. Corrección de endogeneidad: con IV vs. sin IV"

#: ../source/notebooks/customer_choice/bayesian_blp.ipynb:260004
#: d336e20ee6884cd58eae0c4760e14ddc
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"The headline feature of BLP is the endogeneity correction. When prices "
"are set by firms that observe demand shocks $\\xi_{jt}$, regressing "
"shares on prices without instruments overstates willingness-to-pay "
"(biases $\\alpha$ toward zero). We fit a second model *without* "
"instruments to illustrate the bias. With `price_xi_corr=0.6` in the DGP, "
"the no-IV estimator should recover an $\\alpha$ pulled toward zero."
msgstr ""
"La característica principal de BLP es la corrección de endogeneidad. Cuando "
"los precios los fijan empresas que observan los choques de demanda "
"$\\xi_{jt}$, regresar las cuotas sobre los precios sin instrumentos "
"sobreestima la disposición a pagar (sesga $\\alpha$ hacia cero). Ajustamos "
"un segundo modelo *sin* instrumentos para ilustrar el sesgo. Con "
"`price_xi_corr=0.6` en el DGP, el estimador sin IV debería recuperar un "
"$\\alpha$ arrastrado hacia cero."

#: ../source/notebooks/customer_choice/bayesian_blp.ipynb:300002
#: 93262e50dda34549819f362701add0b1
msgid "6. Price elasticities"
msgstr "6. Elasticidades de precio"

#: ../source/notebooks/customer_choice/bayesian_blp.ipynb:300004
#: af8f2bcfaf6c4718a67223ca638bbcbe
msgid "The closed-form mixed-logit elasticity is"
msgstr "La elasticidad del logit mixto en forma cerrada es"

#: ../source/notebooks/customer_choice/bayesian_blp.ipynb:300006
#: 0ff6a8957a8d435e94b390f987b0a0ac
msgid ""
"\n"
"\\varepsilon_{jk}(m) = \\frac{p_{km}}{s_{jm}} \\cdot \\frac{1}{R}\n"
"\\sum_r \\alpha_{ir}(m) \\cdot s_{jmr} \\bigl(\\delta_{jk} - "
"s_{kmr}\\bigr)\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"\\varepsilon_{jk}(m) = \\frac{p_{km}}{s_{jm}} \\cdot \\frac{1}{R}\n"
"\\sum_r \\alpha_{ir}(m) \\cdot s_{jmr} \\bigl(\\delta_{jk} - s_{kmr}\\bigr)\n"

#: ../source/notebooks/customer_choice/bayesian_blp.ipynb:300011
#: b9b5afe81a654d258b11c17ba14974b7
msgid ""
"where the integral over consumer types reuses the same Halton draws as "
"the likelihood (essentially free). Own-price elasticities sit on the "
"diagonal (negative); cross-price elasticities sit off-diagonal (positive "
"for substitutes). `elasticities(at='mean')` returns the posterior-mean "
"elasticity matrix; `at='samples'` returns the full posterior "
"distribution."
msgstr ""
"donde la integral sobre los tipos de consumidor reutiliza las mismas "
"muestras de Halton que la verosimilitud (esencialmente gratis). Las "
"elasticidades propias de precio están en la diagonal (negativas); las "
"elasticidades cruzadas de precio están fuera de la diagonal (positivas para "
"los sustitutos). `elasticities(at='mean')` devuelve la matriz de "
"elasticidades de la media posterior; `at='samples'` devuelve la distribución"
" posterior completa."

#: ../source/notebooks/customer_choice/bayesian_blp.ipynb:330002
#: 6245e6725bd743d59076399e907d2370
msgid "Posterior distribution of the market-averaged own elasticity"
msgstr ""
"Distribución posterior de la elasticidad propia promediada entre mercados"

#: ../source/notebooks/customer_choice/bayesian_blp.ipynb:330004
#: 4d133ddcdb0c4097ac4df4aca67c711d
msgid ""
"The heatmap above shows the posterior *mean* elasticity per cell. To see "
"the **uncertainty** around each product's own-price elasticity, we "
"average across markets *per posterior sample* and plot the resulting one-"
"dimensional posterior:"
msgstr ""
"El mapa de calor de arriba muestra la *media* posterior de la elasticidad "
"por celda. Para ver la **incertidumbre** en torno a la elasticidad propia de"
" precio de cada producto, promediamos entre mercados *por cada muestra "
"posterior* y graficamos la posterior unidimensional resultante:"

#: ../source/notebooks/customer_choice/bayesian_blp.ipynb:330006
#: 4b67c57a37584fe0a7049ef513fb0ba1
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"\n"
"\\bar{\\varepsilon}_{jj}(s) = \\frac{1}{M} \\sum_m \\varepsilon_{jj}(m, "
"s)\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"\\bar{\\varepsilon}_{jj}(s) = \\frac{1}{M} \\sum_m \\varepsilon_{jj}(m, s)\n"

#: ../source/notebooks/customer_choice/bayesian_blp.ipynb:330010
#: 7129b5ace95243ae9ca8ee3e230701e4
msgid ""
"This produces one value per posterior sample per product: the *typical* "
"own-price elasticity for that SKU across the panel. The result is a clean"
" unimodal posterior whose width reflects joint uncertainty in "
"$\\alpha_r$, $\\sigma_{\\text{random}}$, and $\\xi$. Averaging *per "
"sample* preserves the posterior dependence structure; averaging *after* "
"flattening sample × market would smear the genuine uncertainty across a "
"market-by-market mixture."
msgstr ""
"Esto produce un valor por muestra posterior y por producto: la elasticidad "
"propia de precio *típica* de ese SKU en todo el panel. El resultado es una "
"posterior unimodal limpia cuyo ancho refleja la incertidumbre conjunta en "
"$\\alpha_r$, $\\sigma_{\\text{random}}$ y $\\xi$. Promediar *por muestra* "
"preserva la estructura de dependencia posterior; promediar *después* de "
"aplanar muestra × mercado difuminaría la incertidumbre genuina en una mezcla"
" mercado por mercado."

#: ../source/notebooks/customer_choice/bayesian_blp.ipynb:350002
#: 44176ed6a18742429cd58087b79f060b
msgid "Per-market variation in own-price elasticity"
msgstr "Variación por mercado de la elasticidad propia de precio"

#: ../source/notebooks/customer_choice/bayesian_blp.ipynb:350004
#: cfe977bb733a4017968240aed93790ed
msgid ""
"Averaging across markets hides genuine *cross-market* heterogeneity: the "
"same product can be more elastic in markets where its baseline share is "
"small or its realised price is high. The forest plot below shows the per-"
"market 94 % HDI of `prod_0`'s own-price elasticity — one row per market —"
" using the full posterior."
msgstr ""
"Promediar entre mercados oculta la heterogeneidad genuina *entre mercados*: "
"el mismo producto puede ser más elástico en los mercados donde su cuota base"
" es pequeña o su precio realizado es alto. El gráfico de bosque (forest "
"plot) de abajo muestra el HDI del 94 % por mercado de la elasticidad propia "
"de precio de `prod_0` — una fila por mercado — usando la posterior completa."

#: ../source/notebooks/customer_choice/bayesian_blp.ipynb:350006
#: eb78e42fda91465892cb39620425dca9
msgid ""
"The horizontal spread of the interval *centres* is the structural across-"
"market variation that the market-averaged plot collapsed; the *width* of "
"each interval is per-market posterior uncertainty (typically wider in "
"markets with sparse shares or extreme prices)."
msgstr ""
"La dispersión horizontal de los *centros* de los intervalos es la variación "
"estructural entre mercados que el gráfico promediado colapsó; el *ancho* de "
"cada intervalo es la incertidumbre posterior de cada mercado (típicamente "
"mayor en mercados con cuotas escasas o precios extremos)."

#: ../source/notebooks/customer_choice/bayesian_blp.ipynb:370002
#: a9466f7669bd4f3b89266020874fe739
msgid "7. Counterfactual pricing"
msgstr "7. Fijación de precios contrafactual"

#: ../source/notebooks/customer_choice/bayesian_blp.ipynb:370004
#: b08a73cff18a4c7684089b3a2af79d25
msgid ""
"`counterfactual_shares(price_change=...)` holds the latent demand shock "
"ξ_jt constant (read directly from the posterior) and re-evaluates the "
"share equation at new prices. This is the structurally correct "
"counterfactual: it asks *given the same unobserved market conditions*, "
"what would market shares be at the new prices?"
msgstr ""
"`counterfactual_shares(price_change=...)` mantiene constante el choque "
"latente de demanda ξ_jt (leído directamente de la posterior) y reevalúa la "
"ecuación de la cuota con los nuevos precios. Este es el contrafactual "
"estructuralmente correcto: pregunta *dadas las mismas condiciones de mercado"
" no observadas*, ¿cuáles serían las cuotas de mercado con los nuevos "
"precios?"

#: ../source/notebooks/customer_choice/bayesian_blp.ipynb:370006
#: c5864fb1109d4c699672c809d27d6a47
msgid "We examine a **10 % price hike on the first product**:"
msgstr "Examinamos un **aumento del 10 % en el precio del primer producto**:"

#: ../source/notebooks/customer_choice/bayesian_blp.ipynb:370007
#: a043446e6ff2416b910813d59902074a
msgid "its own share should fall (consumers substitute away)"
msgstr ""
"su propia cuota debería caer (los consumidores sustituyen hacia otros "
"productos)"

#: ../source/notebooks/customer_choice/bayesian_blp.ipynb:370008
#: f74cea95ae7e478e9e14e7b38f057f5c
msgid "rival shares and the outside good should rise"
msgstr "las cuotas de los rivales y del bien externo deberían subir"

#: ../source/notebooks/customer_choice/bayesian_blp.ipynb:420002
#: 3f9da3988fea4fafaa9d9238d75d07a5
msgid "Time-targeted counterfactuals"
msgstr "Contrafactuales dirigidos en el tiempo"

#: ../source/notebooks/customer_choice/bayesian_blp.ipynb:420004
#: 9facfbf572cc454e97be39a4ee00cd79
msgid ""
"Because we constructed the model with `time_col=\"period\"`, the "
"counterfactual API accepts `periods=` and `regions=` coord-label "
"arguments. Use them to scope an intervention to a specific time window or"
" geography."
msgstr ""
"Como construimos el modelo con `time_col=\"period\"`, la API de "
"contrafactuales acepta los argumentos de etiquetas de coordenadas `periods=`"
" y `regions=`. Úselos para acotar una intervención a una ventana de tiempo o"
" a una geografía específica."

#: ../source/notebooks/customer_choice/bayesian_blp.ipynb:420006
#: bcf882d4ab11484bb1c9a0807f72452f
msgid ""
"The cell below applies the same 10% price hike on `prod_0` *only* in "
"periods 10–20. Outside that window the counterfactual shares match the "
"baseline bit-for-bit; inside the window they match the full-panel "
"counterfactual."
msgstr ""
"La celda de abajo aplica el mismo aumento del 10% en el precio de `prod_0` "
"*solo* en los períodos 10–20. Fuera de esa ventana las cuotas "
"contrafactuales coinciden bit a bit con la línea base; dentro de la ventana "
"coinciden con el contrafactual de todo el panel."

#: ../source/notebooks/customer_choice/bayesian_blp.ipynb:440002
#: cc8ad958e0304be18e5a051338bbe7c1
msgid "8. Hierarchical pooling across regions"
msgstr "8. Agrupación jerárquica entre regiones"

#: ../source/notebooks/customer_choice/bayesian_blp.ipynb:440004
#: f34cd923973240eda85333090350df33
msgid ""
"When markets belong to distinct geographic regions, `region_col` "
"activates partial pooling across regions:"
msgstr ""
"Cuando los mercados pertenecen a regiones geográficas distintas, "
"`region_col` activa la agrupación parcial entre regiones:"

#: ../source/notebooks/customer_choice/bayesian_blp.ipynb:440011
#: 65b665ac1d574ffe9054cf0634873a5f
msgid ""
"This is the headline differentiator vs GMM BLP: thin markets are shrunk "
"toward the population mean, which keeps inference stable while still "
"using every data point."
msgstr ""
"Este es el principal elemento diferenciador frente a BLP con GMM: los "
"mercados pequeños se contraen hacia la media poblacional, lo que mantiene "
"estable la inferencia sin dejar de usar cada dato."

#: ../source/notebooks/customer_choice/bayesian_blp.ipynb:440013
#: 963f8fa334d54fa3a9e9d8069285702f
msgid ""
"We generate a 3-region panel with genuine region-level preference "
"heterogeneity (`region_heterogeneity=0.6`) and check that $\\tau_\\alpha$"
" (the between-region SD) has posterior mass away from zero."
msgstr ""
"Generamos un panel de 3 regiones con heterogeneidad genuina de preferencias "
"a nivel de región (`region_heterogeneity=0.6`) y verificamos que "
"$\\tau_\\alpha$ (la desviación estándar entre regiones) tenga masa posterior"
" alejada de cero."

#: ../source/notebooks/customer_choice/bayesian_blp.ipynb:510002
#: 6fb90c422be74e1daf8711070b985748
msgid "9. Interpreting the taste profiles"
msgstr "9. Interpretación de los perfiles de gustos"

#: ../source/notebooks/customer_choice/bayesian_blp.ipynb:510004
#: a1aae4aa2dd6465b97addd6ee7e800fe
msgid ""
"The model integrates over a population of consumer taste types to predict"
" aggregate market shares. Having fit the posterior, we can reverse the "
"question: **which taste types does each market rely on to generate its "
"observed shares?** This is Bayesian backward inference, from aggregate "
"patterns to latent consumer heterogeneity."
msgstr ""
"El modelo integra sobre una población de tipos de gusto de los consumidores "
"para predecir las cuotas agregadas de mercado. Una vez ajustada la "
"posterior, podemos invertir la pregunta: **¿en qué tipos de gusto se apoya "
"cada mercado para generar sus cuotas observadas?** Esto es inferencia "
"bayesiana hacia atrás, de patrones agregados a heterogeneidad latente de los"
" consumidores."

#: ../source/notebooks/customer_choice/bayesian_blp.ipynb:510006
#: 8094a94fe34b48d78897236bda430281
msgid ""
"With three random coefficients each consumer type is a vector "
"$\\bm{\\nu}_i = (\\nu_{\\text{price}}, \\nu_{x_0}, \\nu_{x_1})$. The "
"stacked area chart below sorts consumers along $\\nu_{\\text{price}}$ "
"only and so shows a *price-marginal* view: at each x-coordinate the other"
" two taste dimensions vary across the Halton grid. The fully multi-"
"dimensional buyer characterisation comes from the heatmap further down "
"(Lens 1)."
msgstr ""
"Con tres coeficientes aleatorios, cada tipo de consumidor es un vector "
"$\\bm{\\nu}_i = (\\nu_{\\text{price}}, \\nu_{x_0}, \\nu_{x_1})$. El gráfico "
"de áreas apiladas de abajo ordena a los consumidores solo a lo largo de "
"$\\nu_{\\text{price}}$ y por eso muestra una vista *marginal en el precio*: "
"en cada coordenada x, las otras dos dimensiones de gusto varían a lo largo "
"de la cuadrícula de Halton. La caracterización completamente "
"multidimensional de los compradores proviene del mapa de calor más abajo "
"(Lente 1)."

#: ../source/notebooks/customer_choice/bayesian_blp.ipynb:530002
#: 4707470b3d924c39b3c33cfbe4c0b178
msgid "Reading the results"
msgstr "Lectura de los resultados"

#: ../source/notebooks/customer_choice/bayesian_blp.ipynb:530004
#: 6d849b3524c948a780bd20773c65d8f1
msgid ""
"**Market 36 (avg price 0.35): price has nothing to bite on.** The "
"allocation bands run nearly flat across the entire $\\nu$ axis. Even the "
"most price-sensitive consumers (left edge) still buy inside goods; the "
"outside good (grey) stays thin throughout. When everything costs 35 "
"cents, choice is driven almost entirely by characteristics: prod_1 "
"(orange) dominates, prod_2 (green) is second, prod_0 (blue) is a sliver. "
"A flat logit would fit this market about as well."
msgstr ""
"**Mercado 36 (precio promedio 0.35): el precio no tiene dónde hacer mella.**"
" Las bandas de asignación son casi planas a lo largo de todo el eje $\\nu$. "
"Incluso los consumidores más sensibles al precio (borde izquierdo) siguen "
"comprando bienes internos; el bien externo (gris) se mantiene delgado en "
"todo momento. Cuando todo cuesta 35 centavos, la elección está impulsada "
"casi por completo por las características: prod_1 (naranja) domina, prod_2 "
"(verde) es segundo y prod_0 (azul) es apenas una franja. Un logit plano "
"ajustaría este mercado más o menos igual de bien."

#: ../source/notebooks/customer_choice/bayesian_blp.ipynb:530006
#: 92bd941392b442edb97f02d813420e37
msgid ""
"**Market 4 (avg price 1.51): heterogeneity starts to matter.** The "
"outside good grows noticeably on the left as price-sensitive types exit, "
"and the transition is gradual. Prod_1 still dominates inside demand. The "
"inside/outside split at $\\nu = 0$ (the modal consumer) is roughly 60/40,"
" so most consumers still participate. The slope from left to right tells "
"you $\\sigma_{\\text{random}}$ is doing real work here: different taste "
"types make meaningfully different choices."
msgstr ""
"**Mercado 4 (precio promedio 1.51): la heterogeneidad empieza a importar.** "
"El bien externo crece notablemente a la izquierda a medida que los tipos "
"sensibles al precio salen, y la transición es gradual. Prod_1 sigue "
"dominando la demanda interna. La división entre interno y externo en $\\nu ="
" 0$ (el consumidor modal) es aproximadamente 60/40, de modo que la mayoría "
"de los consumidores aún participa. La pendiente de izquierda a derecha "
"indica que $\\sigma_{\\text{random}}$ está haciendo un trabajo real aquí: "
"distintos tipos de gusto toman decisiones significativamente diferentes."

#: ../source/notebooks/customer_choice/bayesian_blp.ipynb:530008
#: b8a47e79623b4c339f269fa9b13ea1e3
msgid ""
"**Market 7 (avg price 2.06): the cliff.** At $\\nu < 0$ the market is "
"almost entirely outside good. The inside products only emerge for $\\nu >"
" 0$, and prod_2 (green) overtakes prod_1 (orange) as the winner among "
"insensitive types. This is the product-switching effect: prod_2 has "
"better non-price characteristics, but you only see that once price "
"sensitivity stops masking it. The modal consumer allocates ~95% to "
"outside; this is a niche category at this price level."
msgstr ""
"**Mercado 7 (precio promedio 2.06): el precipicio.** Con $\\nu < 0$ el "
"mercado es casi por completo bien externo. Los productos internos solo "
"emergen para $\\nu > 0$, y prod_2 (verde) supera a prod_1 (naranja) como "
"ganador entre los tipos insensibles. Este es el efecto de cambio de "
"producto: prod_2 tiene mejores características no relacionadas con el "
"precio, pero solo se aprecia una vez que la sensibilidad al precio deja de "
"enmascararlo. El consumidor modal asigna ~95% al bien externo; esta es una "
"categoría de nicho a este nivel de precio."

#: ../source/notebooks/customer_choice/bayesian_blp.ipynb:530010
#: 2403a7106b8b4c829f80477e08043222
#, python-format
msgid ""
"**Market 33 (avg price 3.26): luxury niche.** The outside good fills "
"nearly the entire chart until $\\nu > 1.5$ (roughly the top 7% of the "
"price-insensitivity distribution). Only the most extreme insensitive "
"types buy inside goods at all, and even they split narrowly between "
"prod_2 and prod_1. The demand-share table below will show this market "
"drawing ~60%+ of its inside demand from insensitive consumers against a "
"16% population baseline."
msgstr ""
"**Mercado 33 (precio promedio 3.26): nicho de lujo.** El bien externo llena "
"casi todo el gráfico hasta $\\nu > 1.5$ (aproximadamente el 7% superior de "
"la distribución de insensibilidad al precio). Solo los tipos insensibles más"
" extremos compran bienes internos, e incluso ellos se reparten estrechamente"
" entre prod_2 y prod_1. La tabla de cuotas de demanda de abajo mostrará que "
"este mercado obtiene ~60%+ de su demanda interna de consumidores "
"insensibles, frente a una línea base poblacional del 16%."

#: ../source/notebooks/customer_choice/bayesian_blp.ipynb:530012
#: 47bd92562da94029824ba166df56c813
msgid ""
"**The cross-market story.** As average price rises from 0.35 to 3.26, the"
" stacked area transforms from a flat rectangle (homogeneous, "
"characteristics-driven) to a step function (only the insensitive tail "
"participates), and the identity of the winning inside product flips from "
"prod_1 to prod_2 along the way."
msgstr ""
"**La historia entre mercados.** A medida que el precio promedio sube de 0.35"
" a 3.26, el área apilada se transforma de un rectángulo plano (homogéneo, "
"impulsado por las características) a una función escalón (solo participa la "
"cola insensible), y la identidad del producto interno ganador cambia de "
"prod_1 a prod_2 en el camino."

#: ../source/notebooks/customer_choice/bayesian_blp.ipynb:550002
#: 4cafeac451f64981b17ef54ce07ce418
msgid "Who is the average inside-good buyer?"
msgstr "¿Quién es el comprador promedio de bienes internos?"

#: ../source/notebooks/customer_choice/bayesian_blp.ipynb:550004
#: 93dbbd81b91045b9b5f8afafe486ad3c
msgid ""
"The bucketed table above answers \"what fraction of the population at "
"each $\\nu$ band ends up buying inside?\" Inverting the question gives a "
"sharper summary: *given* that a consumer buys inside in market $m$, what "
"is the posterior distribution of their full taste vector?"
msgstr ""
"La tabla por tramos de arriba responde \"¿qué fracción de la población en "
"cada banda de $\\nu$ termina comprando bienes internos?\". Invertir la "
"pregunta da un resumen más preciso: *dado* que un consumidor compra bienes "
"internos en el mercado $m$, ¿cuál es la distribución posterior de su vector "
"de gustos completo?"

#: ../source/notebooks/customer_choice/bayesian_blp.ipynb:550006
#: d91d7db66b4b4b45b447e270975ec15c
msgid ""
"For each posterior sample $s$, market $m$, and random-coefficient "
"dimension $d$,"
msgstr ""
"Para cada muestra posterior $s$, mercado $m$ y dimensión de coeficiente "
"aleatorio $d$,"

#: ../source/notebooks/customer_choice/bayesian_blp.ipynb:550008
#: 3aa6eaf5c16c49f5a85e88458f1ca604
msgid ""
"\n"
"\\bar\\nu_{m,d}^{(s)} \\;=\\; \\frac{\\sum_r \\nu_{r,d} \\cdot "
"s^{\\text{in}}_{m,r}(s)}{\\sum_r s^{\\text{in}}_{m,r}(s)}\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"\\bar\\nu_{m,d}^{(s)} \\;=\\; \\frac{\\sum_r \\nu_{r,d} \\cdot s^{\\text{in}}_{m,r}(s)}{\\sum_r s^{\\text{in}}_{m,r}(s)}\n"

#: ../source/notebooks/customer_choice/bayesian_blp.ipynb:550012
#: 983897838d1840d19b2bbe1cae72f0ea
msgid ""
"where $s^{\\text{in}}_{m,r}$ is the per-draw inside-good probability for "
"consumer type $r$. The result is a posterior over the *average buyer's "
"taste vector* in every market, with uncertainty inherited from $(\\alpha,"
" \\sigma_\\alpha, \\beta, \\sigma_\\beta, \\xi)$. Visualised as a "
"`(market × dimension)` heatmap, each row of the heatmap is the three-"
"component taste profile of a market's typical buyer."
msgstr ""
"donde $s^{\\text{in}}_{m,r}$ es la probabilidad por muestra de comprar un "
"bien interno para el tipo de consumidor $r$. El resultado es una posterior "
"sobre el *vector de gustos del comprador promedio* en cada mercado, con una "
"incertidumbre heredada de $(\\alpha, \\sigma_\\alpha, \\beta, "
"\\sigma_\\beta, \\xi)$. Visualizada como un mapa de calor de `(market × "
"dimension)`, cada fila del mapa de calor es el perfil de gustos de tres "
"componentes del comprador típico de un mercado."

#: ../source/notebooks/customer_choice/bayesian_blp.ipynb:570002
#: 7c74a6692a2a45a19b9a3ae3daaeaa9a
msgid ""
"Each row is a market sorted by avg price; each column is one of the three"
" taste dimensions. Red cells mean buyers in that market score *above-"
"modal* on that taste dimension (so insensitive to price, or with a strong"
" positive preference for the characteristic). Blue cells mean *below-"
"modal* buyers (price-sensitive, or aversive to the characteristic)."
msgstr ""
"Cada fila es un mercado ordenado por precio promedio; cada columna es una de"
" las tres dimensiones de gusto. Las celdas rojas significan que los "
"compradores de ese mercado puntúan *por encima de la moda* en esa dimensión "
"de gusto (es decir, son insensibles al precio o tienen una fuerte "
"preferencia positiva por la característica). Las celdas azules significan "
"compradores *por debajo de la moda* (sensibles al precio o con aversión a la"
" característica)."

#: ../source/notebooks/customer_choice/bayesian_blp.ipynb:570004
#: 52af3cc435a14f2a889ae2fe71e1825f
msgid ""
"A market with a uniform red row is served by consumers who are above-"
"modal on every dimension. A market with mixed colours is served by buyers"
" who are insensitive on one dimension but average on another. This is the"
" multi-dimensional analogue of the scalar \"average buyer $\\nu$\" "
"picture: instead of saying \"this market is served by price-insensitive "
"consumers\", we now say \"this market is served by consumers who are "
"price-insensitive *and* high-$x_0$ preference *and* average on $x_1$\"."
msgstr ""
"Un mercado con una fila uniformemente roja es atendido por consumidores que "
"están por encima de la moda en todas las dimensiones. Un mercado con colores"
" mixtos es atendido por compradores que son insensibles en una dimensión "
"pero promedio en otra. Este es el análogo multidimensional de la imagen "
"escalar del \"$\\nu$ del comprador promedio\": en lugar de decir \"este "
"mercado es atendido por consumidores insensibles al precio\", ahora decimos "
"\"este mercado es atendido por consumidores insensibles al precio *y* con "
"alta preferencia por $x_0$ *y* promedio en $x_1$\"."

#: ../source/notebooks/customer_choice/bayesian_blp.ipynb:570006
#: d37953f1116244ee8955f615fb1bff15
msgid ""
"The price dimension still tracks market price (cheaper markets pull "
"buyers in from the price-sensitive side); the $x_0$ and $x_1$ dimensions "
"reveal substitution patterns the scalar lens hid."
msgstr ""
"La dimensión del precio aún sigue el precio del mercado (los mercados más "
"baratos atraen compradores del lado sensible al precio); las dimensiones "
"$x_0$ y $x_1$ revelan patrones de sustitución que la lente escalar ocultaba."

#: ../source/notebooks/customer_choice/bayesian_blp.ipynb:580002
#: bb8bac47e3e149fd8a30598313aa683c
msgid "How concentrated is the demand?"
msgstr "¿Qué tan concentrada está la demanda?"

#: ../source/notebooks/customer_choice/bayesian_blp.ipynb:580004
#: 1aeeb9576f4d4de18f284e96dd370476
msgid ""
"A second question naturally follows: even within a market, is inside-good"
" demand spread across all consumer types, or carried by a narrow slice?"
msgstr ""
"Surge naturalmente una segunda pregunta: incluso dentro de un mercado, ¿la "
"demanda de bienes internos se reparte entre todos los tipos de consumidor o "
"la concentra una porción estrecha?"

#: ../source/notebooks/customer_choice/bayesian_blp.ipynb:580006
#: 15124fa5dfb94f8c9a993c6f126b7147
msgid ""
"For each (sample, market) we compute the Gini coefficient of the per-"
"consumer-type contributions $s^{\\text{in}}_{m,r}$:"
msgstr ""
"Para cada (muestra, mercado) calculamos el coeficiente de Gini de las "
"contribuciones por tipo de consumidor $s^{\\text{in}}_{m,r}$:"

#: ../source/notebooks/customer_choice/bayesian_blp.ipynb:580008
#: 888175790e194cbbb3bd61650717785c
msgid ""
"\n"
"G_m^{(s)} \\;=\\; \\frac{\\sum_{r,r'} |s^{\\text{in}}_{m,r} - "
"s^{\\text{in}}_{m,r'}|}{2 R \\sum_r s^{\\text{in}}_{m,r}}\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"G_m^{(s)} \\;=\\; \\frac{\\sum_{r,r'} |s^{\\text{in}}_{m,r} - s^{\\text{in}}_{m,r'}|}{2 R \\sum_r s^{\\text{in}}_{m,r}}\n"

#: ../source/notebooks/customer_choice/bayesian_blp.ipynb:580012
#: 5d51ed5902c34f9f8e1a4dac95139ad0
msgid ""
"$G_m = 0$ means every consumer type contributes the same amount (broadly "
"served market); $G_m \\to 1$ means one type carries almost all the demand"
" (niche market)."
msgstr ""
"$G_m = 0$ significa que cada tipo de consumidor contribuye la misma cantidad"
" (mercado atendido de forma amplia); $G_m \\to 1$ significa que un solo tipo"
" concentra casi toda la demanda (mercado de nicho)."

#: ../source/notebooks/customer_choice/bayesian_blp.ipynb:600002
#: a6f93f8881294326a3bbf1d8ddc07b6e
msgid ""
"As average price rises, the Gini climbs from near zero to roughly 0.7. At"
" low prices every consumer type buys inside in similar proportion, so "
"demand is uniformly spread (low Gini). At high prices only the "
"insensitive tail buys, so demand concentrates on a thin slice of consumer"
" types (high Gini). The two lenses tell complementary stories: "
"$\\bar\\nu_m$ says *where* on the $\\nu$ axis the buyers sit; the Gini "
"says *how tightly* they cluster there."
msgstr ""
"A medida que el precio promedio sube, el Gini asciende de casi cero a "
"aproximadamente 0.7. A precios bajos, todos los tipos de consumidor compran "
"bienes internos en proporción similar, de modo que la demanda se reparte "
"uniformemente (Gini bajo). A precios altos, solo compra la cola insensible, "
"de modo que la demanda se concentra en una porción delgada de tipos de "
"consumidor (Gini alto). Las dos lentes cuentan historias complementarias: "
"$\\bar\\nu_m$ dice *dónde* en el eje $\\nu$ se ubican los compradores; el "
"Gini dice *qué tan estrechamente* se agrupan allí."

#: ../source/notebooks/customer_choice/bayesian_blp.ipynb:610002
#: e44b935962ce445b8adc514de6410d93
msgid "10. Summary"
msgstr "10. Resumen"

#: ../source/notebooks/customer_choice/bayesian_blp.ipynb:610004
#: fa390862920549f3ba986734d6b590da
msgid "In this notebook we demonstrated the full BayesianBLP workflow:"
msgstr ""
"En este cuaderno demostramos el flujo de trabajo completo de BayesianBLP:"

#: ../source/notebooks/customer_choice/bayesian_blp.ipynb:610006
#: 629dfbb827694818be7597205b1808bf
msgid ""
"**Data generation** — `generate_blp_panel` with endogenous prices and "
"known truth."
msgstr ""
"**Generación de datos** — `generate_blp_panel` con precios endógenos y "
"verdad conocida."

#: ../source/notebooks/customer_choice/bayesian_blp.ipynb:610007
#: c77fc451856845f9a8074e47f5d79355
msgid ""
"**Prior predictive check** — shares sum to 1; priors cover plausible "
"scanner data."
msgstr ""
"**Chequeo predictivo previo** — las cuotas suman 1; los priors cubren datos "
"de escáner plausibles."

#: ../source/notebooks/customer_choice/bayesian_blp.ipynb:610008
#: e7cbba4d40d64e0ebaf0ca26bbfefb95
msgid ""
"**IV fit** — zero divergences; posterior recovers `α`, `β`, `σ_α` inside "
"the 94% HDI."
msgstr ""
"**Ajuste con IV** — cero divergencias; la posterior recupera `α`, `β`, `σ_α`"
" dentro del HDI del 94%."

#: ../source/notebooks/customer_choice/bayesian_blp.ipynb:610009
#: 432b653cd25e4661aff7a9a36ef66a78
msgid ""
"**Endogeneity bias** — dropping instruments biases `α` toward zero; "
"instruments correct this."
msgstr ""
"**Sesgo de endogeneidad** — eliminar los instrumentos sesga `α` hacia cero; "
"los instrumentos corrigen esto."

#: ../source/notebooks/customer_choice/bayesian_blp.ipynb:610011
#: 749f85805023464894cdb6a524e87e13
msgid ""
"**Elasticities** — own-price negative (−3 to −5 range); cross-price "
"positive; full posterior uncertainty available."
msgstr ""
"**Elasticidades** — la propia de precio es negativa (rango de −3 a −5); la "
"cruzada de precio es positiva; se dispone de la incertidumbre posterior "
"completa."

#: ../source/notebooks/customer_choice/bayesian_blp.ipynb:610013
#: 03592d6888dc47cb9499001992423b5d
msgid ""
"**Counterfactual** — a 10% price hike on one product reduces its share, "
"raises rivals and the outside good, with calibrated posterior "
"uncertainty."
msgstr ""
"**Contrafactual** — un aumento del 10% en el precio de un producto reduce su"
" cuota, aumenta la de los rivales y la del bien externo, con una "
"incertidumbre posterior calibrada."

#: ../source/notebooks/customer_choice/bayesian_blp.ipynb:610015
#: e20a568e5b7243df946f71b7e440b34d
msgid "**Price sensitivity** — implied taste profiles per market"
msgstr ""
"**Sensibilidad al precio** — perfiles de gustos implícitos por mercado"
